{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "6f1c2b6e-7d51-4f0a-9a56-3c7b1d5e0a11",
		"name": "Payment Processing System",
		"description": "End-to-end demo of the payment-processing-system API (INR wallets, ledger-backed transfers, async gateway deposits/withdrawals).\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start PostgreSQL, Redis and Kafka locally, then the Spring Boot app (see README).\n2. Import this collection and `payment-system.local.postman_environment.json`, then select the environment.\n3. Run the folders **in order** with the Collection Runner (or Newman): `00 Health` -> `01 Happy path` -> `02 Negative cases` -> `03 Session`. Folder `04 Rate limit (optional)` is separate and can be skipped.\n\n**How state flows**\nTest scripts store tokens, user ids, account ids, payment id and transfer id as *collection variables*; the environment only holds configuration (`baseUrl`, demo emails, demo password, amounts). Every money-moving POST gets a fresh `Idempotency-Key` (a UUID) generated in its pre-request script.\n\n**Payment polling**\nDeposits return `202 Accepted`; the money is only posted to the ledger after the outbox -> Kafka -> simulated gateway round trip. The `Poll payment ...` requests re-run themselves (via `postman.setNextRequest`) until the payment reaches a terminal status, so they need the Collection Runner / Newman. If you send one by hand, just click Send again until the status is terminal.\n\n**Simulated gateway scenarios** are selected by `amountPaise % 100`: 0-79 succeed, 80-89 fail once then succeed on retry, 90-94 keep failing (-> `REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW`), 95-99 permanent decline (-> `FAILED`).\n\nThe demo password in the environment is a throwaway placeholder for local use only; no real credentials belong in this collection.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{ "key": "token", "value": "{{aliceToken}}", "type": "string" }
		]
	},
